&lt;h2&gt;


  How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built SlothSort using Base44 and a React-based frontend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also explored Ollama integration to investigate using open-weight AI models for file-organization suggestions. However, I haven't connected and tested a real model yet, so local AI inference remains unfinished.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open innovation gives developers the freedom to explore models and tools beyond closed, hosted AI APIs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For SlothSort, a properly configured local model could eventually provide more control over how file information is processed and allow experimentation with different models. This project is an early step toward exploring those possibilities.&lt;/p&gt;

